  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given a data set with $9$ data points and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{9}{x}_{i}=45,$ compute $\\overset{\u2015}{x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{9}{x}_{i}=45,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 45=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
